    -> insensitive to thickness: True
       THE OCEAN IS A HALF-SPACE. There is no free surface here, and
       no water-column reverberation. Reported, not gated: it is a
       structural fact about the background, not a tolerance.

  [F5] with free_surface=True the water column REVERBERATES
       AT FIXED (kx, ky), stepping the thickness by quarter-cycles.
       Fixed k is essential: the two-way phase is 2 w eta_w h_w and
       eta_w varies across the transverse grid, so the INTEGRATED
       table has no single period and cannot be periodic in h_w. An
       earlier draft tested the integrated table and read its
       aperiodicity as a failure; it is a property of the integral.
