==============================================================================
GATE top reflector: PASS
  DEFAULT (free_surface=False): an ocean-bottom fluid-solid interface,
  alive, attenuating, parameterised by the water properties -- but the
  ocean above it is a HALF-SPACE. The stage-1 claim that the free
  surface came for free with the layered background was wrong.
  WITH free_surface=True: the water column is finite and reverberates,
  periodically in the round-trip phase at fixed k, and the flag reaches
  the 3-D table. Use it for any comparison against a solver that
  carries a free surface -- FFTProp does.
  STILL OPEN: the absolute magnitude of either. Existence, attenuation,
  parameterisation and periodicity are all satisfied by a wrongly
  scaled surface too. Arbiter: ocean_bottom.py.
==============================================================================
